From 0671b67481a1eaf61c8db1b19b1834ae130c7a47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:30:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Input: rmi4 - do not fail system suspend after powering off

rmi_i2c_suspend() disables the supplies even when the RMI function
suspend callback fails, then returns that error. The PM core does not
mark a device suspended after a failed callback and skips its resume
callback during unwind. The controller can consequently remain powered
off with its IRQ disabled.

Log the function-suspend failure and return success after powering off,
matching the existing runtime-suspend behavior. This lets system resume
restore power and the IRQ. Correct the suspend warning at the same time.

Adapt Timothy Schmidt's original change 6d3c6c42f7bb to the current Input
fixes tree, where reset-GPIO and panel-follower support are absent. The
original change used Claude assistance; this adaptation and its extracted
callback regression fixture used Codex. No new hardware test is claimed.

Fixes: 946c8432aab0 ("Input: synaptics-rmi4 - support regulator supplies")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5 checkpatch
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6 ASan UBSan
---
 drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_i2c.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_i2c.c b/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_i2c.c
index e11d0acb9b96..5561422bf48e 100644
--- a/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_i2c.c
@@ -295,12 +295,13 @@ static int rmi_i2c_suspend(struct device *dev)
 
 	ret = rmi_driver_suspend(rmi_i2c->xport.rmi_dev, true);
 	if (ret)
-		dev_warn(dev, "Failed to resume device: %d\n", ret);
+		dev_warn(dev, "Failed to suspend device: %d\n", ret);
 
 	regulator_bulk_disable(ARRAY_SIZE(rmi_i2c->supplies),
 			       rmi_i2c->supplies);
 
-	return ret;
+	/* Resume must restore power even if putting the device to sleep failed. */
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int rmi_i2c_resume(struct device *dev)
